A calculator application that uses other .babo modules.
Call sample/math_ops.babo for all math operations via call_babo().
Call sample/string_utils.babo for string formatting via call_babo().

The program takes three arguments: <num1> <num2> <operation>
Operations: add, sub, mul, div, pow, mod, max, min, avg, fancy

For "fancy" operation: compute sum and product using math_ops.babo,
then produce a rich-formatted output showing:
- Both input numbers
- Their sum (via call_babo to math_ops)
- Their product (via call_babo to math_ops)
- Both numbers converted to uppercase words via string_utils.babo (use num2words package)

For simple operations (add, sub, mul, div, pow, mod): use math_ops.babo.
For max/min/avg: compute directly in Python.

Use the rich package for beautiful output formatting.
If no arguments or wrong operation, print usage.
